    "biography": {
      "concept": "First soprano of Lyrenn's Water Choir, aged nine (Act 2)",
      "notes": "Wren Ashby is nine, first soprano of Lyrenn's Water Choir, and the one with the clipboard. The Choir is eleven children in eleven channels who conduct the water by listening harder; strangers find them politely terrifying, and Wren most of all. She talks with her eyes shut, grades everything (including you) on a curve, and does not do 'why', because the Choir doesn't do why, it does toward. Everybody listens wrong at first, she says, and writes it down."
